# Commands and options the CLI defines that the completion leaves out on purpose.
#
# The drift check (zsh .github/workflows/test.zsh --drift-only) reads every
# .command() and .option() out of the installed claude binary and reports the
# ones completions/_claude does not have. Commands marked {hidden:!0} are
# skipped on their own. Everything else that should stay out goes here, one
# name per line. A command is matched by name alone, so `show` here also hides
# a future top-level `show`.

